# React Native + pnpm needs a flat node_modules.
#
# Metro's resolver walks real directories, and several toolchain pieces
# resolve from the PROJECT root rather than from the importing package:
# NativeWind's `jsxImportSource` emits `react-native-css-interop/...`
# into your app files, Expo autolinking scans node_modules for native
# modules, and Reanimated/Worklets patch babel from the root. Under
# pnpm's default symlinked layout those all fail to resolve.
#
# This is the layout Expo documents for pnpm. Don't remove it, and
# don't "fix" a resolution error by adding transitive deps (like
# react-native-css-interop) to package.json by hand.
#
# NOTE: pnpm 11 does NOT read this line — it reads `nodeLinker: hoisted`
# from pnpm-workspace.yaml instead, and ignores this file's setting
# silently. Both spellings are shipped (pnpm 9/10 use this one, pnpm 11
# uses the yaml). If you change one, change the other, or the sandbox
# (pnpm 11) gets a symlinked tree and the web bundle fails to resolve
# react-native-css-interop.
node-linker=hoisted

# NOTE: no registry auth lines belong in this file. This is a PUBLIC
# repo — a FontAwesome Pro token here would leak. Use the free icon set
# bundled with @expo/vector-icons.
